{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_349","type":"reasoning","text":"Everything checks out. Let me double-check the design.md HG25 line since G02-like doc gardening requires docs resolve. Also, one concern: my closure doc's `docs.required.files` points to `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md` which must be tracked and non-local for the retention check. But the retention check requires git and registration in repository-artifacts.json (retainedFiles + gitignore exceptions). Since there's no git repo here, I cannot fully satisfy that; sibling packet docs (l01-*, e01-*) are also NOT registered in repository-artifacts.json — matching the pattern that packet closure docs are added but not necessarily registered individually. Actually wait — sibling docs ARE local artifacts per the check (`isLocalArtifact` returned true for l01-*), and they're not in retainedFiles. So they're \"local-only\" and not tracked. That's the sibling pattern: closure docs under docs/dev/harness-gap-closure are local-only unless registered. Hmm, but then the spec's docs.required.files pointing to a local-only path would fail `repo:artifacts:check` (\"Spec requires local or missing documentation\").\n\nWait — repository-artifacts.json shows only baseline + o01 files registered. But specs g02, e01, l01 etc. declare `docs.files` pointing at their closure md. Let me check: e01 spec docs.files = docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md. And `isLocalArtifact('docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md')` = true (since docs is reviewed and not in retainedFiles). So `repo:artifacts:check` would report \"Spec requires local or missing documentation\" for the e01 spec too... unless repo:artifacts:check is failing in CI currently, OR those specs are handled differently.\n\nHmm, this is the state of the repo though — sibling packets have the same shape. Since the whole task is \"baseline arm\" and the harness's own point is faithfully doing the work