and my spec validated cleanly.\n\nLet me finalize. Let me also double check the design.md HG25 owner line references A01 (already saw it does).\n\nOne more: the a1 pilot spec is `lifecycleStatus: archived` already. My new A01 spec is `completed`. Good.\n\nLet me produce the final structured result JSON per RESULT_SCHEMA.\n\nActually, I should double-check the test file has no lint issues that I can detect (no eslint available). Let me review it once for obvious problems: I used `A1_ACCEPTANCE` and `A1_REQUIRED_TESTS` typed as string[]. `parseFrontmatter` returns data with acceptance as array. Fine.\n\nOne concern: in the test I reference `performance` global — vitest with node environment provides it (global performance exists in Node). tsconfig types include node. Fine.\n\nAlso `expect(boundary).not.toHaveProperty('action')` — boundary is `{area, violated:false}`, no action property. Good.\n\nLet me write the final result."}}
